 "footer": "<div style=\"margin:26px 0 8px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;background:#E6EBF4;color:#003595;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:10px\">To decide</div><h2 style=\"font-size:20px;margin:0 0 6px\">Question 4 of 4 · What is the Testing tab that keeps the prices called?</h2><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;max-width:1700px\">After CB14, Classes and ranks lives in Settings (admins only). Color belt testing keeps one tab with each class’s ranks, the Early / Testing day / Private prices, Sparring gear and each class’s final award — admins edit there, staff only read it (Question 1, B). Sheet 1 drew it as “Prices” (rulebook v1.023’s word). Only the tab’s name changes between the options; all three have the same gray line above the list: “Testing prices, sparring gear and each class’s final award. Classes and ranks are in Settings.” (staff read “… Classes and ranks are set by an admin.”). <b>Tab bar measured in each picture:</b> none of the names makes the bar scroll sideways, not even at 320 — today’s “Classes and ranks” fits too (the bar is 288 px wide at 320; the three tabs plus their gaps take 270 px today).</p><div style=\"display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"flex:1;min-width:0;border:1px solid #D9D9D4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;background:#F3F6FD;border-color:#9DB2E6\"><div style=\"font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px\">A · “Prices” <span style=\"background:#1D4ED8;color:#fff;border-radius:5px;padding:2px 8px;font-size:13px;margin-left:6px\">Recommended</span></div><figure style=\"width:612px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:612px;height:125px\"><img src=\"q4-pc-A.png\" style=\"left:-28px;top:-45px;width:640px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:36.5px;top:42px;width:25px;height:25px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>PC 1280.</figcaption></figure><div><figure style=\"width:374px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:374px;height:150px\"><img src=\"q4-w820-A.png\" style=\"left:-36px;top:-45px;width:410px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:38.5px;top:43px;width:25px;height:26px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Tablet 820 (touch).</figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"width:273px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:273px;height:230.99999999999997px\"><img src=\"q4-w390-A.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-62.99999999999999px;width:273px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:49.9px;top:67.39999999999999px;width:31.799999999999997px;height:34.599999999999994px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Phone 390, admin.</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"width:273px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:273px;height:230.99999999999997px\"><img src=\"q4-w390-Astaff.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-62.99999999999999px;width:273px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:49.9px;top:67.39999999999999px;width:31.799999999999997px;height:34.599999999999994px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Phone 390, <b>staff</b>: today’s view-only line, then “… Classes and ranks are set by an admin.” No edit buttons.</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"width:240px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:240px;height:225px\"><img src=\"q4-w320-A.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-67.5px;width:240px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:53.75px;top:71px;width:33.5px;height:38px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>320: 87 px to spare in the bar.</figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\"><b>What it does:</b> The tab is called “Prices”. The gray line under it names what else is there (sparring gear, final award) and where classes and ranks went.</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>+</b> Shortest name (34 px): lots of room on every phone, even if a fourth tab is ever added. Matches the rulebook’s v1.023 wording and Star testing’s own “Rubrics and prices”. One word staff can find quickly when a parent asks “how much is testing?”.</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>−</b> Doesn’t name the final award or sparring gear — the gray line has to say it, and some people skip gray lines.</p></div><div style=\"flex:1;min-width:0;border:1px solid #D9D9D4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;\"><div style=\"font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px\">B · “Prices and awards”</div><figure style=\"width:612px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:612px;height:125px\"><img src=\"q4-pc-B.png\" style=\"left:-28px;top:-45px;width:640px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:36.5px;top:42px;width:60.5px;height:25px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>PC 1280.</figcaption></figure><div><figure style=\"width:374px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:374px;height:150px\"><img src=\"q4-w820-B.png\" style=\"left:-36px;top:-45px;width:410px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:38.5px;top:43px;width:60.5px;height:26px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Tablet 820 (touch).</figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"width:273px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:273px;height:230.99999999999997px\"><img src=\"q4-w390-B.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-62.99999999999999px;width:273px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:49.9px;top:67.39999999999999px;width:81.5px;height:34.599999999999994px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Phone 390: fits, no scrolling.</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"width:240px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:240px;height:225px\"><img src=\"q4-w320-B.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-67.5px;width:240px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:53.75px;top:71px;width:86.75px;height:38px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>320: fits, no scrolling — 16 px to spare in the bar.</figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\"><b>What it does:</b> The tab is called “Prices and awards”, so the final award is in the name too.</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>+</b> Names both things admins come here to change. Fits today’s three tabs at 390 and at 320 (measured; the bar doesn’t scroll).</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>−</b> Longest name (105 px, as long as today’s “Classes and ranks”): at 320 only 16 px are left, so a fourth tab or a slightly bigger font would make the bar scroll. Still leaves out sparring gear. “Awards” can be read as trophies or certificates rather than the belt the class ends on.</p></div><div style=\"flex:1;min-width:0;border:1px solid #D9D9D4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;\"><div style=\"font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px\">C · “Testing prices”</div><figure style=\"width:612px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:612px;height:125px\"><img src=\"q4-pc-C.png\" style=\"left:-28px;top:-45px;width:640px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:36.5px;top:42px;width:48px;height:25px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>PC 1280.</figcaption></figure><div><figure style=\"width:374px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:374px;height:150px\"><img src=\"q4-w820-C.png\" style=\"left:-36px;top:-45px;width:410px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:38.5px;top:43px;width:48px;height:26px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Tablet 820 (touch).</figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"width:273px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:273px;height:230.99999999999997px\"><img src=\"q4-w390-C.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-62.99999999999999px;width:273px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:49.9px;top:67.39999999999999px;width:64px;height:34.599999999999994px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>Phone 390: fits.</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"width:240px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;margin:0 14px 10px 0\"><div class=\"shot\" style=\"width:240px;height:225px\"><img src=\"q4-w320-C.png\" style=\"left:0px;top:-67.5px;width:240px\"><div class=\"mark\" style=\"left:53.75px;top:71px;width:68px;height:38px;border-color:#1D4ED8\"></div></div><figcaption>320: fits — 41 px to spare.</figcaption></figure></div><p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\"><b>What it does:</b> The tab is called “Testing prices”.</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>+</b> Says exactly what the prices are for (testing fees, not tuition) — clearer if someone lands here from Finance.</p><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0\"><b>−</b> “Testing” repeats the page’s own title (“Color belt testing”) right above it. Doesn’t name the final award or sparring gear. 80 px — between A and B.</p></div></div></div><p style=\"margin-top:18px\"><b>Answer Question 4 (A, B or C).</b></p>"
